          <meta property=\"al:android:package\" content=\"com.linkedin.android\">\n          <meta property=\"al:android:app_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/meghana-adiga-bn_amazon-sde2-interviewexperience-activity-7457469538344017920-Fawr\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:app_store_id\" content=\"288429040\">\n          <meta property=\"al:ios:app_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n\n<!---->\n          <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/al2o9zrvru7aqj8e1x2rzsrca\">\n\n        <script>\n          function getDfd() {let yFn,nFn;const p=new Promise(function(y, n){yFn=y;nFn=n;});p.resolve=yFn;p.reject=nFn;return p;}\n          window.lazyloader = getDfd();\n          window.tracking = getDfd();\n          window.impressionTracking = getDfd();\n          window.ingraphTracking = getDfd();\n          window.appDetection = getDfd();\n          window.pemTracking = getDfd();\n          window.appRedirectCompleted = getDfd();\n        </script>\n\n<!---->\n        \n        \n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n    \n    \n    \n    \n\n    \n\n        \n  <meta name=\"description\" content=\"My Amazon SDE2 interview experience\nI recently went through the Amazon SDE2 interview process. It was a good experience overall, although it did not result in an offer.\n\nRound 1: Online Assessment\nThe assessment had three parts:\n• Coding Challenge (90 mins): 2 questions similar to\nhttps://lnkd.in/gft9UQBN \nhttps://lnkd.in/gXqxdQ4z \n• Work Simulation (15 mins)  \nWork through software development decisions faced by SDEs at Amazon\n• Work Style Surveys (10 mins)  \nQuestions focused on how you approach engineering work and collaboration.\n\nRound 2: Phone screening (60 mins) - This round decides whether you move forward to the onsite/loop interviews.\n1 coding question similar to:\nhttps://lnkd.in/gfYgDssx or\nhttps://lnkd.in/g44VnwGM \nfollowed by 2 follow-ups on the question\n\nLoop Interviews:\nRound 3: Coding – Data Structures &amp; Algorithms  (60 mins)\nhttps://lnkd.in/gjAJMgNT with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 4: Coding – Problem Solving  (60 mins)\nCoding question similar to https://lnkd.in/gYJGT8XU with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 5: Coding – Logical &amp; Maintainable (LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Library Management System, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nRound 6: System Design (HLD + LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Notification Service, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nOptional Candid Chat (30 mins)  \nI got this opportunity to speak with an Amazonian outside hiring team about culture, mentorship, and growth.\n\nLeadership Principle Themes I Encountered\n• Something cool I learned on my own  \n• A missed problem and how I fixed it  \n• Identifying and solving a customer pain point  \n• Handling challenging deadlines  \n• Choosing between multiple solutions  \n• Balancing quality vs speed  \n• Disagreeing with team decisions constructively  \n\nKey Takeaways\n• Strong DSA fundamentals are essential, especially sliding window, greedy, and graph problems.  \n• Leadership Principles are deeply embedded in every round—prepare structured stories.  \n• System design and LLD clarity matter as much as coding at this level.  \n• Clear communication and reasoning, managing time matter more than just getting the correct answer.\n\nHope this helps anyone preparing for Amazon SDE2. \n\n#Amazon #SDE2 #InterviewExperience #SoftwareEngineering\">\n  <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"My Amazon SDE2 interview experience\nI recently went through the Amazon SDE2 interview process. It was a good experience overall, although it did not result in an offer.\n\nRound 1: Online Assessment\nThe assessment had three parts:\n• Coding Challenge (90 mins): 2 questions similar to\nhttps://lnkd.in/gft9UQBN \nhttps://lnkd.in/gXqxdQ4z \n• Work Simulation (15 mins)  \nWork through software development decisions faced by SDEs at Amazon\n• Work Style Surveys (10 mins)  \nQuestions focused on how you approach engineering work and collaboration.\n\nRound 2: Phone screening (60 mins) - This round decides whether you move forward to the onsite/loop interviews.\n1 coding question similar to:\nhttps://lnkd.in/gfYgDssx or\nhttps://lnkd.in/g44VnwGM \nfollowed by 2 follow-ups on the question\n\nLoop Interviews:\nRound 3: Coding – Data Structures &amp; Algorithms  (60 mins)\nhttps://lnkd.in/gjAJMgNT with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 4: Coding – Problem Solving  (60 mins)\nCoding question similar to https://lnkd.in/gYJGT8XU with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 5: Coding – Logical &amp; Maintainable (LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Library Management System, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nRound 6: System Design (HLD + LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Notification Service, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nOptional Candid Chat (30 mins)  \nI got this opportunity to speak with an Amazonian outside hiring team about culture, mentorship, and growth.\n\nLeadership Principle Themes I Encountered\n• Something cool I learned on my own  \n• A missed problem and how I fixed it  \n• Identifying and solving a customer pain point  \n• Handling challenging deadlines  \n• Choosing between multiple solutions  \n• Balancing quality vs speed  \n• Disagreeing with team decisions constructively  \n\nKey Takeaways\n• Strong DSA fundamentals are essential, especially sliding window, greedy, and graph problems.  \n• Leadership Principles are deeply embedded in every round—prepare structured stories.  \n• System design and LLD clarity matter as much as coding at this level.  \n• Clear communication and reasoning, managing time matter more than just getting the correct answer.\n\nHope this helps anyone preparing for Amazon SDE2. \n\n#Amazon #SDE2 #InterviewExperience #SoftwareEngineering\">\n  <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"My Amazon SDE2 interview experience\nI recently went through the Amazon SDE2 interview process. It was a good experience overall, although it did not result in an offer.\n\nRound 1: Online Assessment\nThe assessment had three parts:\n• Coding Challenge (90 mins): 2 questions similar to\nhttps://lnkd.in/gft9UQBN \nhttps://lnkd.in/gXqxdQ4z \n• Work Simulation (15 mins)  \nWork through software development decisions faced by SDEs at Amazon\n• Work Style Surveys (10 mins)  \nQuestions focused on how you approach engineering work and collaboration.\n\nRound 2: Phone screening (60 mins) - This round decides whether you move forward to the onsite/loop interviews.\n1 coding question similar to:\nhttps://lnkd.in/gfYgDssx or\nhttps://lnkd.in/g44VnwGM \nfollowed by 2 follow-ups on the question\n\nLoop Interviews:\nRound 3: Coding – Data Structures &amp; Algorithms  (60 mins)\nhttps://lnkd.in/gjAJMgNT with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 4: Coding – Problem Solving  (60 mins)\nCoding question similar to https://lnkd.in/gYJGT8XU with 2 questions on Leadership Principles\n\nRound 5: Coding – Logical &amp; Maintainable (LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Library Management System, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nRound 6: System Design (HLD + LLD)  (60 mins)\nDesign a Notification Service, followed by 2 Leadership Principle questions\n\nOptional Candid Chat (30 mins)  \nI got this opportunity to speak with an Amazonian outside hiring team about culture, mentorship, and growth.\n\nLeadership Principle Themes I Encountered\n• Something cool I learned on my own  \n• A missed problem and how I fixed it  \n• Identifying and solving a customer pain point  \n• Handling challenging deadlines  \n• Choosing between multiple solutions  \n• Balancing quality vs speed  \n• Disagreeing with team decisions constructively  \n\nKey Takeaways\n• Strong DSA fundamentals are essential, especially sliding window, greedy, and graph problems.  \n• Leadership Principles are deeply embedded in every round—prepare structured stories.  \n• System design and LLD clarity matter as much as coding at this level.  \n• Clear communication and reasoning, managing time matter more than just getting the correct answer.\n\nHope this helps anyone preparing for Amazon SDE2. \n\n#Amazon #SDE2 #InterviewExperience #SoftwareEngineering\">\n\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"#amazon #sde2 #interviewexperience #softwareengineering | Meghana Adiga\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"#amazon #sde2 #interviewexperience #softwareengineering | Meghana Adiga\">\n    <title>#amazon #sde2 #interviewexperience #softwareengineering | Meghana Adiga</title>\n\n      <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n\n    <meta property=\"lnkd:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7457469538344017920\">\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/meghana-adiga-bn_amazon-sde2-interviewexperience-activity-7457469538344017920-Fawr\">\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"LinkedIn\">\n      <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\">\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/c45fy346jw096z9pbphyyhdz7\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/c45fy346jw096z9pbphyyhdz7\">\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@linkedin\">\n    <meta property=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/meghana-adiga-bn_amazon-sde2-interviewexperience-activity-7457469538344017920-Fawr\">\n<!---->      <meta name=\"clientSideIngraphs\" content=\"1\" data-gauge-metric-endpoint=\"/feedcontent-guest/api/ingraphs/gauge\" data-counter-metric-endpoint=\"/feedcontent-guest/api/ingraphs/counter\">\n  \n\n        <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://static.licdn.com/aero-v1/sc/h/91h7zu0jhz7p67rcq86908tc\">\n\n        \n    \n      <script 